=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The reported outage between pc_0_0 (10.0.0.2) and pc_0_1 (10.0.1.2) does not
exist. Direct measurement shows 0% packet loss in both directions with
sub-millisecond round-trip times, and the result is consistent across a full
reachability matrix run.

Every component of the dc_clos_bgp fabric is functioning correctly. All seven
eBGP sessions (leaf–spine and spine–super_spine) are fully Established with
correct peer AS numbers and no idle/active states. Both leaf routers originate
their host subnets into BGP (leaf_router_0_0 → 10.0.0.0/24, leaf_router_0_1 →
10.0.1.0/24) and each receives a valid BGP route to the remote rack. The active
forwarding path for east–west traffic is: pc_0_0 → leaf_router_0_0 →
spine_router_0_1 → leaf_router_0_1 → pc_0_1, with the reverse path
symmetrical. spine_router_0_0 carries valid backup routes in the BGP RIB and
would be promoted immediately on a spine_router_0_1 failure. No route-maps,
prefix-lists, access-lists, or weight/local-pref overrides exist anywhere in
the fabric; all five router configurations are clean eBGP stubs.

Root cause: There is no fault. The user's belief that the maintenance window
broke cross-rack connectivity is a false premise — the network was and is
healthy.

Corrective action: No configuration change is needed. Advise the reporter to
retest from the actual hosts; the perceived outage was likely a transient client-
side issue or a misidentified host IP during the maintenance window.
=== END ===
